IMPORT prelude

-- Home Team Science and Technology Agency Act 2019 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person who meets the Agency: the
-- offence of copying the Agency's symbol (s 8), the secrecy offence (s 31), personal immunity (s 32), officers' liability for a
-- company's or a partnership's offence (ss 40(2), 41(2)), and service of documents (s 42); and, for those inside it, who may be a
-- member (ss 9, 11, 12(1), 14(3)), when appointment, removal and resignation take effect (ss 10(3), 15(3), 16(2)), the term
-- (s 18), losing office and no compensation (s 20), quorum and voting (ss 23, 25), and the 2019 transfer of the Ministry of Home
-- Affairs' Science and Technology Group staff (ss 44, 46).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HTSTAA2019.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; it is
-- marked "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 13/1/2022". The latest amendment annotated in the text and the
-- Legislative History is G.N. No. S 26/2022 (Variable Capital Companies (Consequential Amendments to Other Acts) Order 2022, in
-- force 13 January 2022), which added the company and VCC director disqualifications to s 11(2)(d). The retrieval record says
-- "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026". The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is column-shifted for ss 18-20 and
-- ss 40-43; this encoding follows the BODY's numbering.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0174 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. Most of the Act constitutes a statutory board, so the row is SCOPED to the provisions that bind
-- or protect an individual or business, and to the membership and meeting rules that decide whether an Agency decision was
-- validly made. Not encoded: the definitions beyond those used here (s 2), establishment and incorporation (ss 3, 4), functions
-- and powers (ss 5, 6), ministerial directions and information (s 7), the Chairperson's term and the Deputy's powers (s 12(2),
-- (3)), filling vacancies and acting appointments other than eligibility (ss 13, 14(1), (2)), validity of acts (s 17),
-- remuneration (s 19), meetings, presiding and execution of documents (ss 21, 22, 24, 26), committees (ss 27, 28), the Chief
-- Executive and staff (ss 29, 30), the financial provisions (ss 33-39), the state-of-mind evidence rules (ss 40(1), 41(1)),
-- regulations (s 43), and the transfer of assets, liabilities and records and the rest of the employees' protections (ss 45,
-- 46(2)-(6), 47-49). No regulations made under s 43 were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Home Team Science and Technology Agency Act 2019 -- the Agency and the public`

§§ `8 -- the Agency's symbol`

-- s 8(1): the Agency "has the exclusive right to the use of one or more symbols or representations as the Agency may select or
-- devise". s 8(2): "A person who -- (a) uses, without the prior written permission of the Agency, a symbol or representation
-- identical to the Agency's symbol or representation; or (b) uses a symbol or representation that so resembles the Agency's symbol
-- or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion, shall be guilty of an
-- offence" -- fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both.
--
-- The words put "without the prior written permission of the Agency" in limb (a) only. Limb (b) has no permission exception, so a
-- permitted look-alike is still caught on the words. That is a literal reading; whether an identical symbol also falls within
-- limb (b) is left to the caller's flags.
GIVEN `used a symbol identical to the Agency's` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had the Agency's prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `used a symbol so resembling the Agency's as likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence under section 8` IF
        (`used a symbol identical to the Agency's` AND (NOT `had the Agency's prior written permission`))
    OR  `used a symbol so resembling the Agency's as likely to deceive or confuse`

§§ `31 -- preservation of secrecy`

-- s 31(1): "A member of the Agency, an employee of the Agency, the Chief Executive or a committee member, who has information in
-- his or her capacity as such that would not otherwise be available to him or her, must not intentionally or negligently disclose
-- that information to any person except -- (a) in the performance of the Agency's functions; (b) with the prior authorisation from
-- the Agency to do so; (c) for the purposes of any proceedings for an offence under this Act, or any report of those proceedings;
-- (d) as required by an order of court; (e) in complying with the requirements in this Act for members to disclose interests; or
-- (f) as required of or allowed by ... by or under this Act or any other Act." (2): fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not
-- exceeding 12 months or both.
--
-- The section speaks in the present tense ("A member ... who has information"); it does not say "is or has been". Whether a former
-- member or employee is bound is not said; the flag below asks only whether the person held one of the listed positions when the
-- information was obtained, which is an inference. An outsider (a contractor's employee, say) is not listed.
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `is a member, employee, Chief Executive or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information came in that capacity and was not otherwise available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disclosed intentionally or negligently` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the performance of the Agency's functions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with the Agency's prior authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for proceedings for an offence under the Act or a report of them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as required by an order of court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in disclosing a member's interests as the Act requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as required or allowed by or under any Act` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception in section 31(1) applies` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `in the performance of the Agency's functions`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `with the Agency's prior authorisation`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `for proceedings for an offence under the Act or a report of them`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `as required by an order of court`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `in disclosing a member's interests as the Act requires`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `as required or allowed by or under any Act`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under section 31` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `is a member, employee, Chief Executive or committee member`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `the information came in that capacity and was not otherwise available`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `disclosed intentionally or negligently`
    AND (NOT `an exception in section 31(1) applies` `the disclosure`)

§§ `32 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 32: "No liability shall lie against any member, any committee member, the Chief Executive or any employee of the Agency, or
-- any other person acting under the direction of the Agency, for anything which is done or purported to be done, or omitted to be
-- done, in good faith and with reasonable care in -- (a) the exercise or purported exercise of any power of the Agency; or (b) the
-- performance or purported performance of any function of the Agency." Both good faith AND reasonable care are needed: a careless
-- act in good faith is not protected. The Agency itself "may sue and be sued in its corporate name" (s 4(1)(c)).
GIVEN `is a member, committee member, Chief Executive, employee or person acting under the Agency's direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in exercising a power or performing a function of the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is protected from personal liability` IF
        `is a member, committee member, Chief Executive, employee or person acting under the Agency's direction`
    AND `acted in good faith`
    AND `acted with reasonable care`
    AND `acted in exercising a power or performing a function of the Agency`

§§ `40(2), 41(2) -- officers and partners guilty of the organisation's offence`

-- s 40(2): "Where a corporation commits an offence under this Act, a person -- (a) who is -- (i) an officer of the corporation; or
-- (ii) an individual involved in the management of the corporation and in a position to influence the conduct of the corporation
-- in relation to the commission of the offence; and (b) who -- (i) consented or connived, or conspired with others, to effect the
-- commission of the offence; (ii) is in any other way, whether by act or omission, knowingly concerned in, or is party to, the
-- commission of the offence by the corporation; or (iii) knew or ought reasonably to have known that the offence by the corporation
-- (or an offence of the same type) would be or is being committed, and failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent or stop the
-- commission of that offence, shall be guilty of that same offence". s 41(2) is the same for an unincorporated association (its
-- officers and governing-body members) or a partnership (its partners). s 40(5), 41(5): this "applies whether or not the
-- corporation is convicted".
GIVEN `the organisation committed an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an officer, partner or influential manager` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consented, connived or conspired` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was knowingly concerned in or party to it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or ought reasonably to have known of it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable steps to prevent or stop it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is guilty of the same offence` IF
        `the organisation committed an offence under the Act`
    AND `is an officer, partner or influential manager`
    AND (    `consented, connived or conspired`
         OR  `was knowingly concerned in or party to it`
         OR  (`knew or ought reasonably to have known of it` AND (NOT `took all reasonable steps to prevent or stop it`)))

§§ `Penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `using the Agency's symbol (s 8(2))`
    `unauthorised disclosure (s 31(2))`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using the Agency's symbol (s 8(2))` THEN 10000
    WHEN `unauthorised disclosure (s 31(2))` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using the Agency's symbol (s 8(2))` THEN 6
    WHEN `unauthorised disclosure (s 31(2))` THEN 12

§§ `42 -- service of documents`

-- s 42(2): an individual may be served personally, "by sending it by prepaid registered post", by leaving it with an adult at the
-- residential or business address, by affixing a copy there, by fax, or "by sending it by email to the individual's last email
-- address"; (3), (4) give similar lists for partnerships and bodies corporate.
-- s 42(5): "Service ... takes effect -- (a) if the document is sent by fax and a notification of successful transmission is
-- received -- on the day of transmission; (b) if the document is sent by email -- at the time that the email becomes capable of
-- being retrieved by the person to whom it is sent; and (c) if the document is sent by prepaid registered post -- 2 days after the
-- day the document was posted (even if it is returned undelivered)."
-- s 42(6): "service of any document under this Act on a person by email may be effected only with the person's prior consent".
-- s 42(7): "This section does not apply to documents to be served in proceedings in court."
--
-- Days are counted as day numbers. For email the encoding takes the day the email became capable of being retrieved as supplied by
-- the caller. For personal delivery, leaving and affixing, s 42(5) is silent; the encoding takes the day of delivery, which is an
-- inference. A fax with no notification of successful transmission falls outside s 42(5)(a); it is not modelled.
DECLARE `Method of service` IS ONE OF
    `personal delivery`
    `prepaid registered post`
    `fax with notification of successful transmission`
    `email`
    `leaving it at the address`
    `affixing it at the address`

GIVEN `the method` IS A `Method of service`,
      `the addressee consented to email service beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the document is for court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `service under section 42 is available` IF
        (NOT `the document is for court proceedings`)
    AND CONSIDER `the method`
        WHEN `email` THEN `the addressee consented to email service beforehand`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the method` IS A `Method of service`, `the day sent, delivered or retrievable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day service takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `prepaid registered post` THEN `the day sent, delivered or retrievable` PLUS 2
    OTHERWISE `the day sent, delivered or retrievable`

§ `Home Team Science and Technology Agency Act 2019 -- membership and decisions`

§§ `9 -- size of the Agency`

-- s 9(1): "The Agency consists of at least 8 and not more than 20 members." (2): "One of the members (who is not the Chairperson)
-- may be the Chief Executive."
GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency's size is within section 9` IF
    `number of members` AT LEAST 8 AND `number of members` AT MOST 20

§§ `11(2), 12(1), 14(3) -- who may be a member, Chairperson or acting member`

-- s 11(2): "the following individuals are disqualified from being a member of the Agency: (a) an undischarged bankrupt or an
-- individual who has an arrangement with any of his or her creditors; (b) a Judge or judicial officer; (c) an individual who has
-- been sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 6 months or more, and has not received a free pardon; (d) an individual who is"
-- disqualified, under the Companies Act 1967 or the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018 or by a court order under them, from acting
-- as a director or taking part in management "during the period of disqualification"; "(e) an individual who lacks capacity in
-- respect of his or her duties as a member within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act 2008, or in respect of whom an order is made
-- under section 10 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act 2008."
-- "Has an arrangement" is present tense: a past arrangement that has ended is read as no bar (a reading). There is no general bar for
-- a conviction for dishonesty, unlike some older statutory-board Acts; only the length of the sentence counts.
-- s 14(3): an individual "is ineligible for appointment under this section to act as the Chairperson or a member of the Agency if
-- the individual is disqualified under section 11(2)".
-- s 12(1)(a): the Minister may appoint "a member (other than the Chief Executive) to be the Chairperson".
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a Judge or judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `longest prison sentence in months` IS A NUMBER
    `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is within a period of company or VCC director disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lacks capacity as a member or is under a Mental Health Act section 10 order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is disqualified from being a member` IF
        `the candidate`'s `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `has an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is a Judge or judicial officer`
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `longest prison sentence in months` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is within a period of company or VCC director disqualification`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `lacks capacity as a member or is under a Mental Health Act section 10 order`

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate may be appointed to act under section 14` IF
    NOT `the candidate is disqualified from being a member` `the candidate`

-- The Chairperson must already be a member; a disqualified member would have ceased to hold office (s 20(1)(c)), so
-- disqualification is checked too.
GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate may be appointed Chairperson` IF
        `the candidate`'s `is a member`
    AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `is the Chief Executive`)
    AND (NOT `the candidate is disqualified from being a member` `the candidate`)

§§ `10(3), 15(3), 16(2) -- when appointment, removal and resignation take effect`

-- s 10(3): the instrument of appointment must state "(b) the date the appointment takes effect, which must not be a date earlier
-- than the date the instrument is received by the member." s 15(1): the Minister may "at any time and without giving any reason,
-- remove a member"; (3): the notice "must state the date the removal takes effect, which must not be a date earlier than the date
-- the notice is received by the member." s 16(2): "The resignation is effective when the notice in subsection (1) is received by
-- the Minister or at any later time specified in the notice." Days are day numbers; for a resignation with no later time stated,
-- the caller passes 0 as the specified day.
GIVEN `the effective day stated` IS A NUMBER, `the day the member received it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stated effective date is permitted` IF
    `the effective day stated` AT LEAST `the day the member received it`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the later of` MEANS IF `x` AT LEAST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `the smaller one` IS A NUMBER, `the other one` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `the smaller one` AT MOST `the other one` THEN `the smaller one` ELSE `the other one`

GIVEN `the day the Minister received the notice` IS A NUMBER, `the day specified in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day the resignation takes effect` MEANS
    `the later of` `the day the Minister received the notice` `the day specified in the notice`

§§ `18 -- term of appointment`

-- s 18(1): "each member of the Agency holds office for a period of 3 years or any shorter period specified in the instrument of
-- appointment." (2): "A member of the Agency may be re-appointed." s 10(3)(a) requires the instrument to state the term. A period
-- longer than 3 years in the instrument is read as capped at 3 years (36 months); that is a reading of "or any shorter period".
GIVEN `the term in months stated in the instrument` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term in months` MEANS `the lesser of` `the term in months stated in the instrument` 36

§§ `20 -- vacation of office, and no compensation`

-- s 20(1): "A member of the Agency ceases to hold office if he or she -- (a) dies; (b) is adjudicated a bankrupt or makes an
-- arrangement with any of his or her creditors; (c) becomes otherwise disqualified from being a member under section 11(2); (d) is
-- removed from office in accordance with section 15; (e) resigns in accordance with section 16; (f) fails, without reasonable cause,
-- to disclose any interest required under Division 1 of Part 4 of the Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018 and a notice is given
-- under that Act to the Minister about that default; (g) fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the Agency without the approval of
-- the Agency; or (h) is not re-appointed when his or her term of office expires."
-- s 20(2): "A member of the Agency is not entitled to any compensation or other payment or benefit relating to his or her ceasing,
-- for any reason, to hold office as a member."
DECLARE `Member's position` HAS
    `died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adjudicated bankrupt or made an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `otherwise disqualified under section 11(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `removed under section 15` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resigned under section 16` IS A BOOLEAN
    `failed without reasonable cause to disclose an interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a notice of that default was given to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive meetings missed without the Agency's approval` IS A NUMBER
    `term expired without re-appointment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the position` IS A `Member's position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member ceases to hold office` IF
        `the position`'s `died`
    OR  `the position`'s `adjudicated bankrupt or made an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  `the position`'s `otherwise disqualified under section 11(2)`
    OR  `the position`'s `removed under section 15`
    OR  `the position`'s `resigned under section 16`
    OR  (`the position`'s `failed without reasonable cause to disclose an interest` AND `the position`'s `a notice of that default was given to the Minister`)
    OR  `the position`'s `consecutive meetings missed without the Agency's approval` AT LEAST 3
    OR  `the position`'s `term expired without re-appointment`

GIVEN `the position` IS A `Member's position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is entitled to compensation for leaving office` IF FALSE

§§ `23, 25 -- quorum and voting`

-- s 23(1): "The quorum is the number that is one-third the number of members of the Agency." (2): "No business may be transacted at a
-- meeting of the Agency if a quorum is not present." There is no floor of 3, and the Act does not say how a fraction is treated;
-- the encoding requires at least one-third present (in effect rounding up). That is an inference.
-- s 25(1): "Each member of the Agency has one vote." (2): the member presiding "has, in the case of an equality of votes, a casting
-- vote." (3): "A resolution of the Agency is passed if it is agreed by all members present without dissent, or if a majority of the
-- members who are entitled to vote on the matter cast votes in favour of it." (4): "A member present at a meeting ... is presumed to
-- have agreed to, and to have voted in favour of, a resolution ... unless he or she expressly dissents from or votes against the
-- resolution at the meeting or is prevented from voting by section 26 of the Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018."
--
-- Readings: votes in favour are the members present less those who dissent and those prevented (s 25(4)); "the members who are
-- entitled to vote on the matter" is read as all members of the Agency not prevented from voting, present or not, which the caller
-- supplies; on an equality of votes for and against, a casting vote for the resolution adds one vote in favour. All three are
-- readings, not the words.
DECLARE Meeting HAS
    `members of the Agency` IS A NUMBER
    `members present` IS A NUMBER
    `members present who dissent or vote against` IS A NUMBER
    `members present prevented from voting` IS A NUMBER
    `members entitled to vote on the matter` IS A NUMBER
    `the presiding member casts the casting vote in favour` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the meeting` IS A Meeting
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the quorum is present` IF
    `the meeting`'s `members present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `the meeting`'s `members of the Agency`

GIVEN `the meeting` IS A Meeting
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the votes in favour` MEANS
    `the meeting`'s `members present` MINUS `the meeting`'s `members present who dissent or vote against`
        MINUS `the meeting`'s `members present prevented from voting`

GIVEN `the meeting` IS A Meeting
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the votes in favour with any casting vote` MEANS
    IF `the votes in favour` `the meeting` EQUALS `the meeting`'s `members present who dissent or vote against`
       AND `the meeting`'s `the presiding member casts the casting vote in favour`
    THEN `the votes in favour` `the meeting` PLUS 1
    ELSE `the votes in favour` `the meeting`

GIVEN `the meeting` IS A Meeting
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resolution is passed` IF
        `the quorum is present` `the meeting`
    AND (    `the meeting`'s `members present who dissent or vote against` EQUALS 0
         OR  `the votes in favour with any casting vote` `the meeting` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `the meeting`'s `members entitled to vote on the matter`)

§ `Home Team Science and Technology Agency Act 2019 -- the 2019 transfer of staff`

§§ `44, 46(1), (2) -- who was transferred, and no payment for it`

-- s 44: "transferring employee" means any individual who, on the eve of the transfer date, "is a public officer holding a post in the
-- Science and Technology Group of the Ministry of Home Affairs, but does not include any individual whose name is on the list of
-- excluded individuals approved by the Minister"; s 2: "transfer date" means 1 December 2019.
-- s 46(1): on the transfer date every transferring employee "stops being an employee of the transferor" and becomes an employee of
-- the Agency "on terms no less favourable than those enjoyed by the employee on the eve of the transfer date". (2): the transfer
-- "(a) does not interrupt continuity of service; (b) does not constitute a retrenchment or redundancy; and (c) does not entitle any
-- employee so transferred to any payment or other benefit merely because he or she stops being employed by the transferor."
-- (5): "section 18A of the Employment Act 1968 does not apply". (The "no less favourable" test is quoted, not encoded: the Act gives
-- no measure for comparing terms.) "The eve of the transfer date" is read as 30 November 2019, the day before; an inference.
GIVEN `was a public officer in the Science and Technology Group on 30 November 2019` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was on the Minister's list of excluded individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual was transferred to the Agency` IF
        `was a public officer in the Science and Technology Group on 30 November 2019`
    AND (NOT `was on the Minister's list of excluded individuals`)

GIVEN `was transferred to the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer counts as a retrenchment or redundancy` IF FALSE

GIVEN `was transferred to the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer entitles the employee to a payment` IF FALSE
